From 62766372026267afa777375d3ef70fd5c1819f1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 23:01:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/35] Enable expandable_segments: /dev/zero was 2.9x GPU
 usage

smaps on n82 at peak: 59.22 GB of /dev/zero per rank against only 20.3 GB
of GPU memory. Eight ranks x 59 GB = 474 GB, matching the node's 477 GB
shared. The mapping is not a 1:1 mirror of device memory -- the excess is
caching-allocator fragmentation holding many discrete segments, which
expandable_segments:False maximises. Dropped max_split_size_mb:256 with it,
since capping split size compounds fragmentation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wiESxhziDrnsLnG9aizTd
---
